augustus had initiated the third phase  of roman history the empire and he had  provided a model for how it would be  organized Tiberius his successor then  kept things running relatively smoothly  this lecture will trace the fortunes of  the Roman Empire over the next two  centuries and the rulers of this era  will feature both Rome's wisest and most  conscientious Emperor's and several of  its most notorious and really deranged  tyrants the next Emperor to take the  throne was one of the latter a nephew of  Tiberius known by the nickname Caligula  which meant literally Little Boots and  these were actual boots given to him as  a young boy when he had accompanied his  father on military campaigns and he wore  a miniature pair of legionary boots  Caligula was still very very young when  he became Emperor and he rapidly  embarked on a what we might call a reign  of terror and also of profligate  expenditure and just to give you a sense  of the sort of person he was  for entertainment he liked to watch  people being tortured to death whenever  he kissed his wife he would whisper in  her ear you know I could have this  beautiful throat cut any time I please  his favorite saying was let everybody  hate me so long as they fear me and  finally how do you think the ruler of  the known world spent his idle free time  well at least according to one source he  would spend hours every day in front of  a mirror practicing making horrible and  disgusting faces now he did share one  thing in common with the average Roman  he was a fan of horse and chariot racing  and he had a favorite horse which he  named Incitatus it translates literally  to something like speedy Caligula had a  special marble stable built for in  cetanas and on race days he would  stationed troops all around the area  with orders to kill anyone who made  noise just to make sure that Incitatus  got a good night's rest and it was  rumored that Caligula planned to have in  citta toss his horse appointed to the  consulship well after about four years  of these sorts of actions Caligula was  murdered by the commanders of his own  bodyguard who finally just got fed up  with his behavior Caligula though is the  first disastrous result of augustus  decision to base succession on the  principle of heredity but he won't be  the last
 

